[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-3596"] :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-4x+7}\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-4x+7 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+({2}^{2}-{2}^{2})+7 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2})-4+7 \\\\  & =(x-2)^{2}+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-4x+7}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{(x-2)^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{1+((x-2)/\\sqrt{3})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{3}}).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-4x+7}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{1+((x-2)/\\sqrt{3})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{3}})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-49934/selection/a128b48cc3781976b7aa644b74847036e8fb6891a23c28001be394bf01132cf4" :answer/id #uuid "6bd58941-c2c6-554d-a0e9-8b28c1443d18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{11}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x+11}{\\sqrt{3}})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49934/selection/ca3aa8db1dcbb10961e50a748140166cb03fa920322ff5c922400b54b807f9e5" :answer/id #uuid "c2ff6f25-d1d8-55eb-b328-8d2b7c6b8388" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x-3}{\\sqrt{11}})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49934/selection/d67f5433171380b2527fa11842e03cb724f53ef880e5922b609ed19c408df5b8" :answer/id #uuid "1bbb7a7f-19c2-50a4-8450-2ebf6d3b5c9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{33}}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x+3)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49934/selection/24f00b3eaed032dd6aa24648d10e490055afa62045e6aaff94d0a25375126ed0" :answer/id #uuid "5c76b7bb-5703-55ca-8b4c-e73f92ae4c4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x+3}{\\sqrt{11}})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49934/selection/f6e196e20207e4d1d2f8e599351dd7159f7476ecc91563df353d1bae84cc0108" :answer/id #uuid "6fd5663b-3b3d-5e09-ae35-bf44c00519b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x+3}{11})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49934/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd5cbb3a-5475-593b-988d-5f986996eea0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49934/selection/24f00b3eaed032dd6aa24648d10e490055afa62045e6aaff94d0a25375126ed0" :answer-field/choices ["q-49934/selection/a128b48cc3781976b7aa644b74847036e8fb6891a23c28001be394bf01132cf4" "q-49934/selection/ca3aa8db1dcbb10961e50a748140166cb03fa920322ff5c922400b54b807f9e5" "q-49934/selection/d67f5433171380b2527fa11842e03cb724f53ef880e5922b609ed19c408df5b8" "q-49934/selection/24f00b3eaed032dd6aa24648d10e490055afa62045e6aaff94d0a25375126ed0" "q-49934/selection/f6e196e20207e4d1d2f8e599351dd7159f7476ecc91563df353d1bae84cc0108"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49934" :question/id #uuid "05179cbf-a52b-578c-91d6-1ae5539de82e" :question/math-academy-id "q-49934" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-3{x}^{2}-18x+6}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}^{2}-18x+6 & =-3({x}^{2}+6x-2) \\\\  & =-3({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+[{3}^{2}-{3}^{2}]-2) \\\\  & =-3({(x+3)}^{2}-11) \\\\  & =3(11-{(x+3)}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above in the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-3{x}^{2}-18x+6}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3(11-{(x+3)}^{2})}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{33(1-(x+3)^{2}/11)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{33}\\cdot \\sqrt{1-(x+3)^{2}/11}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{33}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((x+3)/\\sqrt{11})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(\\frac{x+3}{\\sqrt{11}}).$  \n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{x+3}{\\sqrt{11}}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{11}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{11}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-3{x}^{2}-18x+6}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{33}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((x+3)/\\sqrt{11})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{33}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot \\sqrt{11}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x+3}{\\sqrt{11}})+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-49934/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db6e4cf3-803a-5942-9ce0-7047942e078a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49934"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-270043/selection/26734acc4349599b013ff5890611204a590e31e398b69a9ba8c4c553e3de6e98" :answer/id #uuid "f77e5da2-41a6-5747-8bf6-ce061656b42d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-270043/selection/adbad78d33491a071139fe589fefda7e9ba65cf97ebbcae14d252ac90459e198" :answer/id #uuid "a3482f5d-bce5-5c29-882a-cfa3432ec756" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-270043/selection/94786ff5da18eca7b34968478ef0ca21ee840249e1ca4e89186df64931ae3be0" :answer/id #uuid "5ce1119b-3908-54d7-85f2-671cc1186580" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-270043/selection/e5c63bc832c49e18fb2678001d953240c26767b2f942793f012ef9f6442d3680" :answer/id #uuid "8011dd0b-6f93-52f0-be2c-df2da4e582e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-270043/selection/aebcffa36ef09b29449f0f11f4b6214dfd7ed25d5380e19ce22b24da27ea26b8" :answer/id #uuid "e96a6ce2-eefc-5350-9afc-1fc349551f40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-270043/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f2683787-d1f3-57a7-9a62-1b306bac0cfd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-270043/selection/aebcffa36ef09b29449f0f11f4b6214dfd7ed25d5380e19ce22b24da27ea26b8" :answer-field/choices ["q-270043/selection/26734acc4349599b013ff5890611204a590e31e398b69a9ba8c4c553e3de6e98" "q-270043/selection/adbad78d33491a071139fe589fefda7e9ba65cf97ebbcae14d252ac90459e198" "q-270043/selection/94786ff5da18eca7b34968478ef0ca21ee840249e1ca4e89186df64931ae3be0" "q-270043/selection/e5c63bc832c49e18fb2678001d953240c26767b2f942793f012ef9f6442d3680" "q-270043/selection/aebcffa36ef09b29449f0f11f4b6214dfd7ed25d5380e19ce22b24da27ea26b8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-270043" :question/id #uuid "2b9411ac-ea97-5e1c-9757-3b199c7513a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-270043" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{-1-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{1-2x-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2x-{x}^{2} & =1-({x}^{2}+2x) \\\\  & =1-({x}^{2}+2x+1-1) \\\\  & =1-((x+1)^{2}-1) \\\\  & =2-(x+1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{1-2x-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{2-(x+1)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{2(1-(x+1)^{2}/2)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{1-(x+1)^{2}/(\\sqrt{2})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{2}}{\\int }_{-1-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((x+1)/\\sqrt{2})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(\\frac{x+1}{\\sqrt{2}}).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=(\\frac{x+1}{\\sqrt{2}}).\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-1-\\sqrt{2}/2$ | $-1+\\sqrt{2}/2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-1/2$ | $1/2$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{1+2x-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{2}}{\\int }_{-1-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((x+1)/\\sqrt{2})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{2}}{\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}u. \\\\  & =14{\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =14\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u\\,{|}_{-1/2}^{1/2} \\\\  & =14(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =14(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\  & =\\frac{14\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-270043/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db6e4cf3-803a-5942-9ce0-7047942e078a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-270043"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348532/field-1/29ec2dfefa1bd3742bf5ba922b9c261dd5f2325bd8484e9153eb979dbd6eced6" :answer/id #uuid "4c1ba5e8-56a7-56c6-a719-0e74f223e78a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348532/field-1/f37b140e44c3c1469a0b674232c5aaeb4f71e6e7b8d79e0c213b062c66caacc7" :answer/id #uuid "d66372c1-338b-5f5d-91ca-97a24d50562a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348532/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "aa43e869-ffd8-534e-bab9-31a347265593" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348532/field-1/29ec2dfefa1bd3742bf5ba922b9c261dd5f2325bd8484e9153eb979dbd6eced6" :answer-field/choices ["q-348532/field-1/29ec2dfefa1bd3742bf5ba922b9c261dd5f2325bd8484e9153eb979dbd6eced6" "q-348532/field-1/f37b140e44c3c1469a0b674232c5aaeb4f71e6e7b8d79e0c213b062c66caacc7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348532" :question/id #uuid "7a0a72f7-fdec-5ce0-ade3-a046bfe26695" :question/math-academy-id "q-348532" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{4+\\sqrt{2}}^{6}\\frac{12}{|x-4|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8x+15}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square for the expression inside the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8x+15 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4x+({4}^{2}-{4}^{2})+15 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2})-16+15 \\\\  & =(x-4)^{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{4+\\sqrt{2}}^{6}\\frac{12}{|x-4|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8x+15}}\\,\\text{d}x=12{\\int }_{4+\\sqrt{2}}^{6}\\frac{1}{|x-4|\\sqrt{(x-4)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x-4).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x-4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $4+\\sqrt{2}$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\sqrt{2}$ | $2$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4+\\sqrt{2}}^{6}\\frac{12}{|x-4|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8x+15}}\\,\\text{d}x & =12{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{2}\\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =12\\,\\text{arcsec}\\,u\\,{|}_{\\sqrt{2}}^{2} \\\\  & =12(\\text{arcsec}(2)-\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{2})) \\\\  & =12(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-348532/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d1dc808-1ee6-5037-b53e-9e1e4686a11c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348532"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348553/field-1/f37b140e44c3c1469a0b674232c5aaeb4f71e6e7b8d79e0c213b062c66caacc7" :answer/id #uuid "042725ef-c815-51c0-bee5-0d7e7a31f3b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348553/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6bcb229c-b6e9-5f9a-ad69-0deda754e10f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348553/field-1/f37b140e44c3c1469a0b674232c5aaeb4f71e6e7b8d79e0c213b062c66caacc7" :answer-field/choices ["q-348553/field-1/f37b140e44c3c1469a0b674232c5aaeb4f71e6e7b8d79e0c213b062c66caacc7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348553" :question/id #uuid "e8bcf7d0-5de5-553f-a324-8d00997d674e" :question/math-academy-id "q-348553" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-3}^{\\sqrt{3}-3}\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+6x+10}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+6x+10 & ={x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+({3}^{2}-{3}^{2})+10 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2})-9+10 \\\\  & =(x+3)^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+6x+10}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{6}{(x+3)^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x+3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x+3).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x+3.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $\\sqrt{3}-3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ |\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{\\sqrt{3}-3}\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+6x+10}\\,\\text{d}x & =6{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =6(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\sqrt{3}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =6(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0) \\\\  & =2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-348553/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6aa497df-853e-5e77-9d43-6183fa53ffff"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348553"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
